607,'Conflicting Solver'),(2608,'Collect Order Group This category is used for Movement Groups in Builders.'),(2609,'Bank Account Type This category represents bank account type such as saving account, checking account, etc.'),(2610,'Agent Privilege'),(2611,'Agent'),(2612,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.\n\n  This movement group is used to group movements that have the same\n  variation property dict.'),(2613,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2614,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2615,'A Telephone object can contain a telephone number.'),(2616,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2617,'Solver Tool contains Solver Types'),(2618,'Rounding Tool'),(2620,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2621,'A Role Definition allows for associating a certain Zope role to a list of users, organisations, domains, etc.'),(2622,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2624,'A Query allows for capturing questions of users about ERP5 documents. It can be used as a collaboration tool, for sharing knowledge or to provide online help.'),(2625,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2626,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2627,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2628,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2629,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2630,'Holds person objects'),(2631,'Persons capture the contact information (ex. name, phone number) and the relation between entities (ex. who is assigned to which function and which organisation). Persons are supported by a standard validation workflow.'),(2632,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2633,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2634,'Holds organisation objects'),(2635,'Organisations capture the contact information (ex. name, phone number) and their classification (ex. site, group, function etc.). Organisations are supported by a standard validation workflow.'),(2637,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2638,'Delivery Builder objects allow to gather multiple Simulation Movements\n    into a single Delivery. \n\n    The initial quantity property of the Delivery Line is calculated by\n    summing quantities of related Simulation Movements.\n\n    Delivery Builders are called for example whenever an order is confirmed.\n    They are also called globaly in order to gather any confirmed or above \n    Simulation Movement which was not associated to any Delivery Line. \n    Such movements are called orphaned Simulation Movements.\n\n    Delivery Builder objects are provided with a set a parameters to achieve \n    their goal:\n\n    A path definition: source, destination, etc. which defines the general \n    kind of movements it applies.\n\n    simulation_select_method which defines how to query all Simulation \n    Movements which meet certain criteria (including the above path path \n    definition).\n\n    collect_order_list which defines how to group selected movements \n    according to gathering rules.\n\n    delivery_select_method which defines how to select existing Delivery \n    which may eventually be updated with selected simulation movements.\n\n    delivery_module, delivery_type and delivery_line_type which define the \n    module and portal types for newly built Deliveries and Delivery Lines.\n\n    Delivery Builders can also be provided with optional parameters to \n    restrict selection to a given root Applied Rule caused by a single Order\n    or to Simulation Movements related to a limited set of existing \n    Deliveries.'),(2641,'Messages that can be seen by the user and that appear depending upon the actions of the user. They can be warning, information or error messages'),(2642,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2643,'This movement group gathers movements which their start_date and stop_date are in the same month.'),(2644,'Mapped Property object describes how properties or categories are mapped from simulation movements to delivery documents, eg. use source as destination, use destination as source, use quantity as -quantity, etc.'),(2645,'A URL allows to represent in a standard way coordinates such as web sites, emails, ftp sites, etc.'),(2646,'This movement group is used to collect movements related to the same invoice. This movement group should be used in delivery level.'),(2647,'Image type documents in ERP5. Many formats are supported'),(2648,'A Geographical Location represent a point on the surface of the Earth which is address by its coordinates. Geographical Location'),(2649,'A Geographical Area represent an area of the Earth which is address by its Geographical Points. Geographical Area'),(2650,'A file, in its widest sense'),(2651,'A fax number that can be stored on a person or organisation document'),(2653,'Holds Embedded File. Embedded Folder'),(2654,'An embedded file (which can act as an image as well). Embedded File'),(2655,'An Email object can contain a link to an online resource.'),(2657,'Delivery Type is a Base Type which allows its portal type instances to define a list of ledger to which they can belong to. Delivery Type'),(2660,'Like CausalityAssignmentMovementGroup, but using the delivery relation of\nsimulation movements instead of order relation. This is intended to be used in deeper level of simulation tree.'),(2661,'XXX Deprecated. It must be deleted. 2 new portal types replace it: Generated Delivery Builder and Simulated Delivery Builder\n\nDelivery Builder objects allow to gather multiple Simulation Movements into\na single Delivery. The initial quantity property of the Delivery Line is\ncalculated by summing quantities of related Simulation Movements.\n\nDelivery Builders are called for example whenever an order is confirmed.\nThey are also called globally in order to gather any confirmed or above\nSimulation Movement which was not associated to any Delivery Line.  Such\nmovements are called orphaned Simulation Movements.\n\nDelivery Builder objects are provided with a set a parameters to achieve\ntheir goal:\n\nA path definition: source, destination, etc. which defines the general\nkind of movements it applies.\n\nsimulation_select_method which defines how to query all Simulation\nMovements which meet certain criteria (including the above path path\ndefinition).\n\ncollect_order_list which defines how to group selected movements according\nto gathering rules.\n\ndelivery_select_method which defines how to select existing Delivery  which\nmay eventually be updated with selected simulation movements.\n\ndelivery_module, delivery_type and delivery_line_type which define the\nmodule and portal types for newly built Deliveries and Delivery Lines.\n\nDelivery Builders can also be provided with optional parameters to\nrestrict selection to a given root Applied Rule caused by a single Order or\nto Simulation Movements related to a limited set of existing Deliveries.'),(2662,'This movement group is used to group movements which belong to the same day'),(2663,'Holds Accounting Transaction objects'),(2664,'This line can define the value of a currency towards another currency'),(2665,'Une ligne tarifaire.'),(2666,'A Currency is a resource which can be credited or debited on general ledger accounts. It defines currency information, identification and exchange rates to one or multiple reference currencies.'),(2667,'A credit registered in a bank and that can be used for a payment'),(2668,'A chat address is an identifier in an Instant Messaging service.'),(2669,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2670,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2671,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2672,'A step in the career of a person.'),(2673,'The purpose of MovementGroup is to define how movements are grouped,\n  and how values are updated from simulation movements.'),(2674,'A bank account number holds a collection of numbers and codes (ex. SWIFT, RIB, etc.) which may be used to identify a bank account. It is owned by a Person or an Organisation. A Bank Account contains Agents with Agent Privileges used by the owner to delegate the management of the bank account to trusted third-party Persons.\n\nBankAccount inherits from Base and from the mix-in Coordinate.'),(2675,'An Assignment allows a person to be assigned to an organisation during a period without changing his career organisation.'),(2676,'An Agent Privilege allows the Bank Account owner to give permissions to an Agent for a given period of time, for a maximum amount of money.'),(2677,'An Agent is a Person who is permitted to perform some actions on the bank account according to Privileges.'),(2678,'A geographic address holds the geographic address of a person or company.'),(2679,'Solvers'),(2680,'Solver Processes'),(2681,'Rounding Tool'),(2682,'PersonLoginMigration'),(2683,'BaseMigration'),(2684,'BarcodeUtils'),(2696,'Login'),(2697,'GeographicalPoint'),(2698,'GeographicalArea'),(2699,'erp5_base'),(2700,'erp5_base ERP5 Base includes base module for the most common use of ERP5: Organisations, Persons and Currencies.'),(2711,'Notification Message'),(2713,'Notification Messages'),(2722,'Movement Group'),(2731,'Movement Group'),(2736,'Mapped Property'),(2744,'Login'),(2747,'Full Size Image'),(2753,'Image'),(2758,'Geographical Location'),(2763,'Geographical Location'),(2773,'Geographic Address'),(2780,'Field Library for File and Images'),(2785,'File'),(2791,'External Identifier'),(2798,'Entity Field Library'),(2809,'Document'),(2817,'Email'),(2827,'Update Content from URL'),(2829,'Migrate Type'),(2830,'Download Original File'),(2844,'Split and Defer'),(2858,'Portal Type'),(2860,'Delivery Builders'),(2871,'Profile'),(2876,'Predicate Group'),(2894,'Delivery Builder'),(2902,'Currency Field Library'),(2911,'Currency'),(2916,'Currencies'),(2928,'Currency Exchange Line'),(2945,'Credit Card'),(2948,'Coordinate Field Library'),(2965,'Career Field Library'),(2984,'Career'),(2990,'Post Query'),(2997,'Mobile Telephone Coordinate'),(3004,'Query'),(3006,'Folder Contents'),(3015,'Movement Group'),(3024,'Movement Group'),(3032,'Movement Group'),(3036,'Base'),(3040,'Change Password'),(3049,'Person Detailed Report'),(3054,'Person Details'),(3058,'Events'),(3060,'Contributions'),(3080,'Civil Status'),(3085,'Careers'),(3090,'Financial Information'),(3107,'Person Field Library'),(3134,'Details'),(3139,'Create User'),(3148,'Person Assignment View'),(3174,'Person'),(3198,'Persons'),(3208,'Financial Information'),(3227,'Organisation Field Library'),(3244,'Organisation'),(3263,'Organisation'),(3268,'Organisations'),(3271,'Profile'),(3290,'Order Builder'),(3295,'Notification Message'),(3299,'Notification Message Contents'),(3508,'URL'),(3516,'Address Field Library'),(3528,'Telephone'),(3543,'Solver Configuration'),(3558,'Portal Type'),(3566,'Solver Process'),(3568,'Configuration'),(3574,'Solver Decision'),(3576,'Rounding Models'),(3584,'Rounding Model'),(3591,'Role Definition Field Library'),(3595,'View'),(3602,'Liability'),(3603,'Income'),(3604,'Expense'),(3605,'Equity'),(3606,'Asset'),(3607,'Collected VAT'),(3608,'Payable'),(3609,'Liability'),(3610,'Income'),(3611,'Expense'),(3612,'Equity'),(3613,'Refundable VAT'),(3614,'Receivable'),(3615,'Bank'),(3616,'Cash'),(3617,'Asset'),(3618,'Check Payable and Receivable Accounts Grouped Check that all transactions on payable and receivable accounts for which balance is 0 are grouped together'),(3619,'Check Accounting Grouping Reference Validity Check that accounting transaction lines grouped together have a 0 balance'),(3620,'Accounts'),(3621,'Accounting'),(3622,'General Accounting Plan'),(3623,'Financial Section'),(3624,'Account Type WARNING: do not modify Ids for this base category. Id is used in many places in accounting. This base category should be read-only.\nYou can still safely change Title or (better) translate it using Localizer'),(3625,'Those lines belong to Sale Invoice Transactions and can be generated either when the related Sales Packing List is delivered, or by the accountant manually. Those lines will generate the accounting transaction lines of the accounting transaction.'),(3626,'A Sale Invoice Transaction combines in the same document a customer invoice and the accounting transaction deriving from it. Sale Invoice Transactions are normally generated automatically by ERP5 simulation from delivered Sale Packing Lists or groups thereof. They may also be entered by human intervention to fit specific invoicing cases. Accounting transaction lines are generated automatically out of invoice lines through business rules yet can be modified by accountants to fit specific accounting cases.'),(3627,'Those lines belong to Purchase Invoice Transactions and can be generated either when the related Sales Packing List is delivered, or by the accountant manually. Those lines will generate the accounting transaction lines of the accounting transaction.'),(3628,'A Purchase Invoice Transaction combines in the same document a supplier invoice and the accounting transaction deriving from it. Purchase Invoice Transactions are normally generated automatically by ERP5 simulation from delivered Purchase Packing Lists or groups thereof and are set in planned state. Upon reception of a paper invoice, it is the task of the accountant to match it to an expected invoice in planned state or to enter it manually. Accounting transaction lines are generated automatically out of invoice lines through business rules yet can be modified by accountants to fit specific accounting cases.'),(3629,'Incoming payment and outgoing payment transactions that can be done from the accounting module.'),(3630,'Payment Simulation Rule object make sure an Payment in the simulation is consistent with the real payment.'),(3631,'Invoice Root Simulation Rule object makes sure an Invoice in the simulation is consistent with the real invoice.'),(3632,'Those lines belong to Purchase Invoice Transactions and can be generated either when the related Sales Packing List is delivered, or by the accountant manually. Those lines will generate the accounting transaction lines of the accounting transaction.'),(3633,'A Purchase Invoice Transaction combines in the same document a supplier invoice and the accounting transaction deriving from it. Purchase Invoice Transactions are normally generated automatically by ERP5 simulation from delivered Purchase Packing Lists or groups thereof and are set in planned state. Upon reception of a paper invoice, it is the task of the accountant to match it to an expected invoice in planned state or to enter it manually. Accounting transaction lines are generated automatically out of invoice lines through business rules yet can be modified by accountants to fit specific accounting cases.'),(3634,'A machine that tabulates the amount of sales transactions, makes a permanent and cumulative record of them, and has a drawer in which cash can be kept.'),(3635,'Line of Balance Transaction'),(3636,'Balance Transaction'),(3637,'Accounting Transaction Root Simulation Rule object makes sure an Accounting Transaction in the simulation is consistent with the real accounting transaction.'),(3638,'Holds Accounting Transaction objects'),(3639,'Accounting transaction lines are generated either from invoice lines, or created manually by the accountant. Each line correspond to a credit or debit of a specific account for a given transaction, for instance, a sale invoice transaction will most of the time have 3 accounting lines: 1 for the client account, one for the sold goods account, and one for the VAT account.'),(3640,'An Accounting Transaction Balance Constraint checks whether accounting transaction total debit and total credit are equal'),(3641,'An accounting transaction, created from scratch by the accountant or whoever entitled to create transactions in ERP5'),(3642,'Mark the beginning and the end of an Accounting Period.\nOnce the period is closed (i.e. the Accounting Period Delimiter is in delivered state), it is no longer possible to validate Transaction in this period'),(3643,'A Category Existence Constraint checks whether an object contains the given categories without or with Acquisition'),(3644,'A Category Existence Constraint checks whether an object contains the given categories without or with Acquisition'),(3645,'Holds Account objects'),(3646,'An Account defines a legislation independent general ledger account which can hold multiple amounts of currencies. It can be mapped to any number of national accounting nomen